{"n": 1069, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "1069.webp", "text": "Procedures;\n\n1. Place repair patches on the damaged surface and hold them In position with\nadhesive tape. Cul out patches and roof skin together with a saddier's knife\n(at right angles to the surface being repaired).\n\n2. Remove old cement and clean the repair surtace.\n\n3. Repair damaged point In the honeycomb structure with a fiber tiller and\nharden with an ultraviolet light. in case of deeper damage apply the filler in\nlayers and then harden with an ultraviolet light. Then apply a cqat of final\nfiller and harden with an ultraviolet light.\n\n4. Grind and clean repair surtace.\n\n5. Mix cement and hardener In ratio of 15 to 1.\n\n6. Apply a thin coat of the mixed cement on the repalr surface and back of\npatches,\n\n7. Allow about 15 minutes drying time for the cement.\n8. Apply patches (edges butted) and press on firmly with a rubber roller.\n\nimportant!\napplicable, remove any cement squeezed oul on the sides (don't smear It!).\n\n9. Dip a glass rod In Plastisol and coal the bull edges thoroughly.\n10. Allow about 15 minutes drying time for the butt edges.\n\n11. Clean part of or the entire hardtop wilh an alcoholic solution (2 %) or walery\nsolution on soap basis.\n\n12. Paint part of or the entire hardtop with clear lacquer.", "words": [["Procedures;", 0.0338, 0.0805, 0.0999, 0.095], ["1.", 0.0348, 0.1162, 0.0429, 0.1254], ["Place", 0.0525, 0.1149, 0.0817, 0.1267], ["repair", 0.0858, 0.1149, 0.115, 0.1294], ["patches", 0.1191, 0.1149, 0.2523, 0.1307], ["on", 0.1655, 0.1122, 0.1776, 0.1347], ["the", 0.1826, 0.1122, 0.2003, 0.1347], ["damaged", 0.2053, 0.1149, 0.2503, 0.1307], ["surface", 0.2558, 0.1122, 0.2962, 0.1347], ["and", 0.3012, 0.1122, 0.3189, 0.1347], ["hold", 0.3244, 0.1122, 0.3461, 0.1347], ["them", 0.3512, 0.1122, 0.3734, 0.1347], ["In", 0.3784, 0.1122, 0.3905, 0.1347], ["position", 0.3951, 0.1162, 0.4384, 0.1307], ["with", 0.443, 0.1162, 0.4662, 0.1281], ["adhesive", 0.0515, 0.